"explanation": "The documents provide conflicting estimates for the population of Moyale depending on whether the term refers specifically to the town or the broader administrative woreda (district) and the year of the census. \n\n1. **25,038**: Documents 1, 3, and the extracted evidence state that based on the 2005 Central Statistical Agency figures, the town of Moyale had an estimated population of 25,038.\n2. **128,016**: Document 2 states that the 'woreda' (administrative district) containing Moyale had an estimated total population of 128,016 in 2005. It explicitly notes that 25,038 (the town population) constitutes 19.56% of this larger figure.\n3. **254,137**: Documents 7 and 8 report that based on the 2007 Census conducted by the Central Statistical Agency of Ethiopia, the woreda had a total population of 254,137.\n\nSince the question asks for the 'estimated total population of Moyale' without specifying the year or the administrative scope (town vs. woreda), all three figures found in the text are valid answers representing different contexts (Town 2005, Woreda 2005, Woreda 2007)."
}

